      "evidence": "template/scripts/agent_friction.py resolve_positional_id (candidate.diff lines 377-395) raises FrictionLogError unconditionally. It is called from read_state and read_attributions, which review-path and record_checkpoint also use. The spec says tolerance applies to review-path output and to an accepted `friction-log` gap (spec.md line 22), and design.md decision 3 says the same. Resolution by line number also gives a wrong target silently if an earlier line was removed. The spec scenario 'earlier line was removed' only covers content ids, so this is an edge case rather than a contradiction.",
      "id": "positional-resolution-ignores-gap-context",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "resolve_positional_id always reads the log strictly. It does not honor tolerate_local_gap, so review-path and checkpoints with an accepted friction-log gap can still fail on an unreadable log or an invalid line N whenever route state or attributions hold legacy-N keys."
    }
